  "term": "micropolygyria",
  "definition": "Micropolygyria is a group of brain cortex malformations in which there are too many unusually small, partly fused folds, shallow grooves, and abnormal layering of the cortex. It is understood as arising from abnormal later-stage development of neurons in the cerebral cortex and is associated with epilepsy and learning difficulties.",
